     'A daddy chaser is drawn to partners who present as daddies, which may mean older, larger, more established or more dominant depending on the community. Unlike silver fox, the term usually carries a suggestion of role as well as appearance.'),
    ('pantyboy', 'Pantyboy', 'expression-presentation', 'concept', true, true, true,
     'A man or masculine person who wears women''s underwear, often as part of kink or self-expression.',
     'Pantyboy describes a man or masculine-presenting person who wears panties, whether privately, as part of a feminisation dynamic, or simply because he likes them. It is a self-descriptor as often as it is a role assigned in play, and it says nothing on its own about the wearer''s gender or orientation.'),
    ('boywife', 'Boywife', 'expression-presentation', 'concept', false, false, true,
     'A feminine or submissive masculine partner occupying a wife-like role.',
     'Boywife is an internet-native term for a masculine-presenting person, often young and queer, who takes a domestic or feminine partner role. It is used mostly as affectionate self-description and plays on the mismatch between "boy" and "wife" rather than asserting a gender identity.'),
    ('side-piece', 'Side Piece', 'relationship-structures', 'concept', false, false, true,
     'A secondary partner outside someone''s primary relationship.',
     'Side piece refers to a person someone is involved with alongside a main relationship. In common use it usually implies the primary partner does not know, which distinguishes it from the negotiated secondary partners of consensual non-monogamy. The term is informal and often dismissive.'),
    ('thot', 'Thot', 'slang-terminology', 'concept', false, true, true,
